### Source Code
All analysis scripts, Python modules, and software components contained in this repository are released under the MIT License.

### Research Materials and Documentation
The following materials are made available under the Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International License (CC BY 4.0), unless otherwise stated:
* **S1 Appendix:** Bilingual Study Questionnaire (Arabic & English)
* **S2 Appendix:** Data Cleaning, Exclusion Flow, and Sensitivity Analyses (Includes Response Bias Assessment & Dual Sensitivity Analyses)
* **S3 Appendix:** Statistical Analysis Plan (SAP v2.1) and Data Codebook
* **S4 Appendix:** Qualitative Analysis of Open-Ended Responses (Q30)
* **S5 Appendix:** (Withdrawn / Expunged — Preliminary Medicinal Plant Safety Database)
* **S6 Appendix:** STROBE Statement Checklist for Cross-Sectional Studies
* **S7 Appendix:** CHERRIES Checklist for Web-Based E-Surveys
* **S8 Appendix:** Institutional Ethics Approval Documentation (SHAMNA-26-04)
* **S9 Appendix:** Reproducibility Guide and Analysis Environment Specification
* **Primary Dataset:** Anonymized Primary Dataset (`Anonymized_Dataset_N_287.csv`, N = 287)

Users are free to copy, distribute, adapt, and reuse these materials provided appropriate attribution is given to the original authors.

### Data Availability
The anonymized dataset (`Anonymized_Dataset_N_287.csv`, N = 287) contains no personally identifiable information (with 13 underage respondents excluded from the raw N = 300 sample) and is provided to facilitate transparency, reproducibility, secondary analyses, and educational use.

### Ethical Considerations
Data sharing is consistent with the informed consent obtained from participants and the ethical approval granted by the Biomedical Ethics Committee of the Syrian Herbs & Alternative Medicine Association (SHAMNA), Syria.

**Approval Number:** SHAMNA-26-04  
**Approval Date:** 10 April 2026  

All participant information was anonymized prior to public release. No attempt should be made to identify individual participants.

### Citation Requirement
Users of the dataset, questionnaire, codebook, supplementary materials, or analysis workflow are requested to cite the associated manuscript and Zenodo archive:

> Khatib C, Abo Kaf T, Masri THF, Mathbout N, Zayat Y. *Exploratory Survey of Herbal Medicine Use and Safety Awareness among Digitally Connected Syrian Adults: Implications for Arabic Digital Health Resources.* Revised for PLOS ONE (2026).  
> **Zenodo Repository DOI:** https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.20777941

• **Source Code License:** MIT License (Permissive open-source code reuse).  
• **Research Documentation & Data License:** Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International (CC BY 4.0).  
• **Statistical Analysis Plan (SAP v2.1):** Pre-specified bivariate chi-square tests, Yates' continuity correction for 2x2 tables, Fisher's exact tests, Monte Carlo simulations (10,000 iterations, seed 20260415) for sparse tables, Odds Ratios with 95% CIs, Cramér's V effect sizes, and dual sensitivity analyses (N=286 duplicate-excluded and N=258 pilot-excluded).
